    <h2>FAQ<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <details><summary>What is the till code in Rooms &amp; Exits Chapter 2 Level 7?</summary><p><b>350</b>. You do not find it written anywhere: it is the level of the smoothie you blend at the juice bar. Fill the blender until the red drink sits on the <b>350 ml</b> line, then type 350 on the register keypad at the counter and press the green arrow.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What is the computer code in the Food Court?</summary><p><b>53402</b>. The monitor on the back counter, behind the coffee bar, opens a QWERTY keyboard and a single input field. Type 53402, confirm, and a <b>Name tag</b> drops into your inventory.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What is the three-letter code at the end of Chapter 2 Level 7?</summary><p><b>ZCO</b>. The last lock is a keyboard with three slots. The table service you assemble carries the three letters in reading order: a <b>Z</b> piped in mustard on the plate, a <b>C</b> in the foam of the coffee, and the round cupcake. Type Z, C, O and the level ends.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Where do I get the payment card?</summary><p>The card is in your inventory, labelled <b>Payment card</b>, and it is in the name of <b>MARIA</b>. The till asks for payment right after you enter 350, and using the card on the register clears the sale. You never have to hunt for it on the floor.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What is the piece of paper numbered 1042 P-23?</summary><p>It is a printed slip that goes into your bag as <b>Piece of paper</b>. The header reads <b>1042 P-23</b> and underneath there are six coloured dots in two rows of three. Our recording never shows it being used on anything, so this page does not claim it opens a lock.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How long does the Food Court take?</summary><p>The recording runs 11 minutes 10 seconds of video and the in-game clock reads <b>17:31</b> on the results screen. Nothing in the level is timed and there is no fail state; the time goes on criss-crossing the court between four kiosks.</p></details>

